                <pb facs="0817" n="697" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg697"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/4320: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-05-02T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 2, 1922—4
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>108. Your telegram, May 1, 11 p.m., no. 187. If Colonel Martin and Admiral
                    Strauss approve, the Department does not object to <pb facs="0818" n="698"
                        xml:id="pg698"/> the substitution of marines for soldiers called for in your
                    telegram of April 29, 3 p.m., no. 177.</p>
                <p>Report any developments of importance, especially any increase by other foreign
                    powers of their military forces and any evidence indicating anti-foreign
                    tendency.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
